---
layout: default
title: Freediving for kids
---

<div class="page mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <header class="mb-16">
    <h1 class="mb-6 mt-0 text-balance text-5xl font-black leading-[0.95] tracking-[-0.05em] sm:text-7xl">Calm starts young.</h1>
    <p class="mb-0 text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-slate-100 sm:text-2xl">Children learn to float, swim, glide and dive with an instructor beside them, one skill at a time.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="max-w-4xl">
    <div class="mb-14">
      <p class="mb-3 text-3xl font-black leading-tight tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-5xl">The dive reflex starts in the pool.</p>
      <p class="page-prose mb-0">Hold your breath in water and your heart slows down on its own. The same response that keeps a diver calm at depth settles a child before a test at school.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-14">
      <p class="mb-3 text-3xl font-black leading-tight tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-5xl">Posture and lung capacity.</p>
      <p class="page-prose mb-0">Sessions build how a child stands and how much air the body can hold.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-14">
      <p class="mb-3 text-3xl font-black leading-tight tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-5xl">Focus that holds.</p>
      <p class="page-prose mb-0">Underwater there is one task. Attention gets quieter and sharper.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-14">
      <p class="mb-3 text-3xl font-black leading-tight tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-5xl">Swim and dive safely.</p>
      <p class="page-prose mb-0">The child learns to swim on the surface, to dive under, and to stay safe in the water.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-14">
      <p class="mb-3 text-3xl font-black leading-tight tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-5xl">Love of the water.</p>
      <p class="page-prose mb-0">The sea is alive. Kids learn to look after it and to leave it as they found it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-14">
      <p class="mb-3 text-3xl font-black leading-tight tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-5xl">One instructor, one child.</p>
      <p class="page-prose mb-0">Full attention. The pace follows this child instead of a group average. Pool first. Open water once the basics are calm and automatic. We take as long as it takes.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-14">
      <p class="mb-3 text-3xl font-black leading-tight tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-5xl">Progress you can see.</p>
      <p class="page-prose mb-0">Kids set small goals and hit them. A longer float. A cleaner duck dive. A quiet recovery after a hold.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-14">
      <p class="mb-3 text-3xl font-black leading-tight tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-5xl">Parents stay in the loop.</p>
      <p class="page-prose mb-0">After sessions we talk through what changed &mdash; comfort in the water, focus, recovery &mdash; so you know how your child is developing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <a href="https://instagram.com/nofinsfreediving" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn mt-6">Let&rsquo;s freedive</a>
</div>
